WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.200
We followed two chains of references from the declaration
named riemannHypothesis in Alpöge’s Lean source.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:15.800
In the proof, the first enters a volume identity and the second
a compatibility condition. This film traces both and checks the bridge.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:21.700
The original archive spans 175,187 modules and reaches almost
1.5 million declarations from riemannHypothesis.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:30.400
Raw caller counts put core Lean plumbing at the top. Filtering out
boilerplate leaves small domain operations like classMass and hecke.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:38.700
Reachability in that frozen build shows what this formalization
actually routed through—not that every RH proof must go this way.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:47.267
In the definition of HeckeAt, rd g is the value being specified.
On the right, ρ.hecke applies the Hecke operator to rd f.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:54.667
That reference gives one edge from HeckeAt to Setup.hecke.
Watch where it sits in the two paths we traced.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:01:02.867
The highlighted reference ends the blue path. Both paths start
at riemannHypothesis and share their first eight links.

00:01:02.867 --> 00:01:11.467
From the fork, the amber branch reaches classMass in 15 links;
the blue branch runs through heckeTieT and HeckeAt in 19.

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:18.267
In part 1, the masses of A and B filled a bar:
1/4 + 1/6 = 5/12.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:27.467
The proof has the same picture with its own data: a volume cut
into one piece per double-coset class, each of size 1 ÷ d.

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:33.967
The theorem volumes_eq_masses_of_unfold uses that decomposition:
the volume equals the sum of the reciprocal symmetry orders.

00:01:33.967 --> 00:01:41.967
And because every omitted class adds positive weight, matching
the volume certifies that a list of classes is complete.

00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:48.167
Keep A’s three neighbours in view. Counting the B destinations
gives the matrix entry 2.

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:57.367
Now read the function at the same neighbours. Its values are
2, −3 and −3. They give the new value at A, which is −4.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:04.767
HeckeAt requires the target value to agree with the normalized
neighbour sum for every certified local input.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:13.067
The series construction copies that setup so it can match forms
to series coefficients. heckeTieT carries the equality straight across.

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:20.767
To check the arithmetic without compiling all 175,187 modules,
the repo separates the standalone Lean kernel from a formal bridge.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:29.367
The bridge ties the rational formulas to Alpöge’s exact definitions,
while 270 replayed entries check row sums, detailed balance, and commutativity.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:36.167
So that is where the two sums enter the proof.
One identifies a volume and pins completeness.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:47.667
The other specifies the value of a transformed form
and survives transport into the series setup.
